    "reasoning": "The Firestore structure is designed to store insemination records and related data (Puskeswan, Breeder, Cow, Straw). The structure prioritizes authorization independence by storing all insemination records under a single collection and denormalizing the relevant information into the insemination record document. This eliminates the need for complex `get()` calls in security rules and enables atomic operations.\n\nThe primary collection is `inseminationRecords`. It stores data about each insemination event. References to other entities (Puskeswan, Breeder, Cow, and Straw) are stored as IDs within the InseminationRecord documents. \n\nThis structure allows for simple, secure `list` operations (QAPs) on the `inseminationRecords` collection, as the rules can be based solely on the data contained within each document.  The denormalization of data contributes to authorization independence, allowing for easier management of access control and data integrity."
